The Health Data Research Service should be backed with sustained, long-term investment and political commitment, with realistic expectations. It should:
• publish a strategy setting out its priority activities and expected timelines, including how it will support broad access to health data for UK researchers and SMEs;
• function as a single front door for access to health data for research held across the NHS and in existing research assets (Biobank and Our Future Health);
• adopt clear metrics for its success and report on them;
• strongly encourage linking primary care data;
• support the build-out of sovereign data capacity, including storing data in UK-based data centres (as discussed in the later report section on Sovereign digital capability in the NHS);
• consider taking on data controllership of key national data assets like GP data.
